<Page title={"About"} description={"Romain Blachier, energy and geopolitics expert, lecturer and columnist. Background, areas of expertise and commitments."} lang="en">
	<h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
	<p class="page-lede">Energy and geopolitics, around one question: who really decides, and with what means.</p>
	<div class="page-body">
<p>I work on energy policy and the governance of the power sector, with two main fields: Central Africa and the Indo-Pacific, Taiwan in particular (energy security, semiconductors, China-Taiwan relations).</p>
<p>One thread runs through all of it: the gap between the authority an institution holds on paper and its actual capacity to act. That holds for a regulator, for a metropolitan authority, for a national utility.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>18 years</strong> in the energy sector (electricity generation).</li>
<li><strong>12 years</strong> as an elected official in the Lyon metropolitan area (culture, digital, international).</li>
<li>Lecturer since 2010: {taught}. Scheduled for 2026-2027: {upcoming}.</li>
<li>Registered energy expert with the African Development Bank.</li>
<li>Associate fellow at the Fondation Jean-Jaurès and member of the civil-society college of the Plateforme RSE (France Stratégie).</li>
<li>President of the France-Formosa Association.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Areas of expertise</h2>
<p>Energy markets and geopolitics, energy transition and sovereignty, Taiwan &amp; Indo-Pacific, comparative political systems, strategic and crisis communications, public affairs.</p>
<h2>Languages</h2>
<p>French (native), English (C1, working language for fieldwork, writing and teaching), Spanish (C1, teaching language: lectures on European politics at the Universidad de Granada), basic Mandarin Chinese.</p>
